perator Points): 150/161 = 0.931677. It is computed over that class and NOT over the claims alone, because a denominator defined by the extractedFrom link itself cannot move when that link is lost: the earlier reading divided by the extraction claims ALONE — the class that link defines — so it read nothing but 1.000000 BY CONSTRUCTION, with the 'other' Points sitting outside it. Whether an unanchored 'other' Point lost a link or was minted by a writer that never derives is the attribution #9736 still owns. #9736 holds BOTH the amendment §10.1 makes and the reopening of the model, and §10.1 reports BOTH readings — the amended denominator and the pre-amendment one — while this row states the amended one's composition, so neither is read off a denominator whose composition was hidden
